Data Structures and Algorithms – Midterm Examination

Question 1 (5 Marks):
What is the time complexity of Binary Search? Explain briefly.

Answer:
Binary Search has a time complexity of O(log n).

It uses the divide-and-conquer approach. In each step, the algorithm compares
the target value with the middle element of the sorted array.

If the target is smaller than the middle element, the search continues in the
left half of the array. If the target is greater, the search continues in the
right half.

Thus, after every comparison, the search space is reduced to half. Because the
number of remaining elements decreases exponentially, the total number of
comparisons grows logarithmically with the size of the input.

Therefore, the overall time complexity of Binary Search is O(log n).